 UK", "agent governance"], "faq": [["What did UK regulators publish on AI cyber risk?", "In November 2026 the Bank of England, PRA and FCA published a consultation on cyber risk and resilience management, CP17/26 and GC26/9, and separate effective practices describing how firms are managing AI-related cyber risk, including reducing their attack surface against AI-enabled attacks."], ["Are effective practices mandatory?", "No. They describe practices regulators consider effective. In practice they become a reference point in supervisory discussions, so firms should know how their own controls compare."], ["Why standardise on one agent framework?", "Controls such as identity, tool access, logging and kill switches can then be built once and applied to every agent, instead of being re-implemented, or forgotten, in each team's own build."]], "related": ["/fractional-cto-united-kingdom/", "/ai-architect/", "/fractional-cto/"], "citations": [{"title": "Effective practices: Cyber risk and resilience management relating to artificial intelligence (AI)", "url": "https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/prudential-regulation/publication/2026/november/effective-practices-cyber-risk-and-resilience-management-relating-to-artificial-intelligence", "publisher": "Bank of England", "date": "Nov 2026"}, {"title": "CP17/26 and GC26/9: Cyber risk and resilience management", "url": "https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/prudential-regulation/publication/2026/november/cyber-risk-and-resilience-management-consultation-paper", "publisher": "Bank of England", "date": "Nov 2026"}, {"title": "PS21/3: Building operational resilience", "url": "https://www.fca.org.uk/publication/policy/ps21-3-operational-resilience.pdf", "publisher": "Financial Conduct Authority", "date": "Mar 2021"}, {"title": "Cyber Assessment Framework", "url": "https://www.ncsc.gov.uk/collection/cyber-assessment-framework", "publisher": "National Cyber Security Centre"}, {"title": "AI Agent Observability: Evolving Standards and Best Practi